      scenario: "Month-end brings apparent good news: payroll is 8% under budget and your director congratulates you in the leadership meeting.\n\nBefore accepting the praise, read the number like a manager. You have carried three unfilled vacancies all month, overtime is up, and two 'rushed treatment' comments have appeared in reviews. Work out what the favourable variance is actually made of, what invoice it will present later, and what you would say in the meeting - knowing that correcting your own good news is precisely what builds a director's trust in your reporting.",
